      "nets": [
        "+5V",
        "VCC"
      ],
      "observed": "U2 is an LM1117-5.0 fixed 5 V linear regulator, but both its input pin (U2.2, VI) and output pin (U2.3, VO) are connected to the same +5V power net. The separate VCC rail is not connected to the regulator input.",
      "expected": "For a 5 V regulator, the input should be connected to the unregulated supply rail (here VCC) and the output should provide the +5V rail. Input and output of the regulator should not be shorted together.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "schematic",
          "quote": "Right tile: U2 LM1117-5.0, pin 2 VI has a +5V power symbol and pin 3 VO has a +5V power symbol; VCC appears elsewhere (e.g. J2/JP2/Q2) but not on U2 input."
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The 5V regulator is bypassed. If VCC is the intended higher input voltage, the MCU/5V rail will not be regulated and may be unpowered or improperly powered; if VCC is also 5V, the regulator serves no purpose and its dropout may reduce the 5V rail.",
      "confidence": 0.8
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The schematic shows a clear anomaly: the LM1117-5.0 regulator input and output are both tied to +5V, shorting the regulator's input and output and bypassing regulation."
}

